50:Malcolm: This is strange, very strange. Kregor has returned to the throne. Dyron's armor has been stolen. The Black Inquisition has been reborn... Something doesn't sit right with me.
51:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: Whether it fits or not, they pose a threat.
52:Malcolm: I don't like the fact that "Guest" with armor and axes simply let me escape from Valtaria.
53:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: So he's planning something. He wants to use Valtaria and Kregor, but we don't know for what purpose yet.
54:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: We have to hurry...
55:[$CC00C0]Commander[$FFFFFF]: My Lord! 
56:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: Yes!? You must have important news if you arrive so out of breath.
57:[$CC00C0]Commander[$FFFFFF]: The army with the light green flag has crossed the Nikos River.
58:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: What are you up to, Kregor... How many are there!?
59:[$CC00C0]Commander[$FFFFFF]: I'm not sure. A few hundred, maybe over a thousand.
60:Malcolm: They want to force their way through Hanrain. The armor was stolen. The city probably defended itself, but no one can stop these weapons. They are powerless. 
61:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: Kregor wants revenge...
62:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: If Hanrain falls, the rest of Artidram will turn to us as the safest place. Then "Guest" and Kregor will get everything here on a silver platter.
63:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: We can't let that happen.
64:Malcolm: So I'll leave you the fight, and I'll go to warn everyone.
65:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: No! Your knowledge is very useful. You can't be exposed to enemy attack.
66:[$E4DFEC]Eryt[$FFFFFF]: Then I'll go.

67:Malcolm: Eryt...
68:[$E4DFEC]Eryt[$FFFFFF]: Don't worry. I'll meet you in Andaro, I'll be waiting for you there.
69:[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: Prepare to march!